  "text": "The angles ${30}^{\u2218}$ and ${45}^{\u2218}$ are special, and their trigonometric ratios have the  values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061{30}^{\u2218}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{tan}\u2061{45}^{\u2218}=1.\n$$\n\nAlso, note that ${tan}^{2}\u2061{30}^{\u2218}$ simply means $(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061{30}^{\u2218})^{2}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{tan}^{2}\u2061{30}^{\u2218}-\\operatorname{tan}\u2061{45}^{\u2218} & = \\\\ 3{(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061{30}^{\u2218})}^{2}-\\operatorname{tan}\u2061{45}^{\u2218} & = \\\\ 3{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})}^{2}-1 & = \\\\ 3(\\frac{3}{9})-1 & = \\\\ 1-1 & = \\\\ 0 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14229290/history-expanded-37263e41a9c354ced7bd.html",
